          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఝరి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఝరి — jhari — \"a stream\" or \"mountain stream\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it in two gentle pieces: jha, ri. Say the word as ఝ-రి. The first sound is a breathy jh; the second piece is the familiar రి."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఝరి (jhari) is an authentic learned or literary word shared with Sanskrit. It is not an everyday word you must force into conversation. Keep its concrete image today: a stream running down a slope."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
