            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One gentle look back first: వాఙ్మయం means \"literature,\" and its uncommon letter is ఙ. Point to ఙ without copying it. Today you will keep that shape distinct from a different uncommon letter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now say ఝరి (jhari) once. What does it mean? (\"A stream\" or \"mountain stream.\")"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now slow the first piece: jha. That breathy jh base letter is today's whole task."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ఝ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఝ — jha."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In ఝరి (jhari), the first base letter is ఝ. The rest, రి, is already familiar. Read the whole word in two pieces: ఝ-రి."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This aspirated letter is uncommon in everyday Telugu vocabulary. That is why the book gave you the authentic word ఝరి (jhari) before asking you to practise the shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ఝ — five movements, five runs",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Follow the filmstrip slowly. Movement 1 circles the broad left bowl. Lift. Movement 2 circles the middle bowl. Lift again. Movement 3 circles the right bowl. Movement 4 sweeps through the separate upper flourish. Movement 5 draws the separate stem downward below the middle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The numbered route is one attested school-style order; Telugu handwriting can vary. Keep all five pen-down runs distinct and let the three bowls stay round."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
